{"step_index":372,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-23T20:19:27Z","thinking":"**Confirming Project Build Success**\n\nFantastic news! I've just successfully built the project using `vite build`, and it completed in a swift 18.36 seconds, entirely error-free! A staggering 1714 modules were efficiently transformed and bundled into the `dist/` directory. Next, I'm setting my sights on crafting a comprehensive `README.md` file, which will be placed in `C:\\Users\\rajan\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\codeduel\\README.md`.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"\"# CodeDuel — Real-Time 1v1 Competitive Programming Platform\\n\\nCodeDuel is a production-oriented, full-stack 1v1 real-time competitive programming platform inspired by modern competitive versus experiences. Two players face off on identical coding problems under a server-authoritative timer, submit code evaluated in an isolated execution sandbox, and are scored based on **Correctness → Execution Efficiency (70%) + Memory (30%) → Submission Speed**.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## ⚡ Tech Stack\\n\\n- **Frontend**: React 18, React Router v6, Tailwind CSS, Monaco Code Editor, STOMP/SockJS WebSockets, Axios, Lucide Icons, Canvas Confetti.\\n- **Backend**: Java 17, Spring Boot 3.2, Spring Security 6, Spring Data JPA, Spring WebSocket, Spring Data Redis, JJWT, Springdoc OpenAPI / Swagger.\\n- **Database**: MySQL 8.0 (with H2 in-memory fallback for zero-dependency development resilience).\\n- **Cache & Real-Time**: Redis 7 (Matchmaking sorted sets, match states, global leaderboards, Pub/Sub).\\n- **Judging Engine**: Subprocess execution sandbox supporting **Java, Python, C++, and JavaScript** with strict CPU, memory, and timeout limits.\\n- **Problem Bank**: 1,000 distinct curated DSA questions with starter codes in 4 languages, constraints, complexity metadata, and test cases.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 🎮 Core Competitive Experience\\n\\n```text\\nFind Opponent → Match Found → 3... 2... 1... GO! → Same Problem → 15:00 Server Timer →\\nCode in Monaco Editor → Run Tests → Submit Solution → Secure Sandbox Judge →\\nCompare Performance & Efficiency → Winner Fanfare → Elo Rating Update → Post-Match Analysis\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 🚀 Quick Start\\n\\n### Option 1: Docker Compose (All Services in 1 Command)\\n\\n```bash\\ncd codeduel\\ndocker-compose up --build\\n```\\n- Frontend UI: `http://localhost:3000`\\n- Backend API & Swagger: `http://localhost:8080/swagger-ui.html`\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Option 2: Local Development\\n\\n#### 1. Start Backend (Spring Boot)\\n```bash\\ncd backend\\nmvn spring-boot:run\\n```\\nThe backend will automatically start on `http:/\n<truncated 3426 bytes>","Description":"\"CodeDuel production documentation and user guide\"","Overwrite":"true","TargetFile":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\rajan\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\scratch\\\\codeduel\\\\README.md\"","toolAction":"\"Creating README.md\"","toolSummary":"\"Write README.md\""}}],"truncated_fields":["tool_calls"]}
